  "published": "2026-04-16T18:36:12.45Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Highlights in this release:\n- Added RFC-aligned request validation for Host, Content-Length, HTTP version, and request-target handling.\n- Added support for all HTTP/1.1 request-target forms: origin-form, absolute-form, authority-form (CONNECT), and asterisk-form (OPTIONS *).\n- Added Transfer-Encoding: chunked request body decoding, trailer parsing, and automatic Expect: 100-continue handling.\n- Added configurable request limits: MaxRequestBodySize (413), MaxRequestTargetSize (414), and MaxRequestHeadersSize (431).\n- Added malformed-version and unsupported-version handling with 400 Bad Request and 505 HTTP Version Not Supported responses.\n- Added correct payload suppression for HEAD and 304 Not Modified responses.\n- Expanded automated coverage with parser, transport, limit, and chunked-body tests.",
